+## Expired updates 
 
 If you don’t take any action after an update fails, Stripe voids the invoice and discards the update after it expires.
 
-A pending update’s `expired_at` time matches the first occurrence of either the [trial end](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions/object.md#subscription_object-trial_end) or the earliest [items.current period end](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions/object.md##subscription_object-items-data-current_period_end). This applies if either time is within 23 hours of the update request. Otherwise, the expiration is 23 hours from the update request.
+A pending update’s `expires_at` time matches the first occurrence of either the [trial end](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions/object.md#subscription_object-trial_end) or the earliest [items.current period end](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions/object.md##subscription_object-items-data-current_period_end). This applies if either time is within 23 hours of the update request. Otherwise, the expiration is 23 hours from the update request.
 
 Stripe also automatically voids the invoice and removes the pending update if any of the following occurs:
 
 - The subscription reaches a billing threshold.
 - A subscription schedule linked to the subscription transitions to a new phase.
+- A later subscription update includes `billing_cycle_anchor`, a nonempty `items` list, `trial_end`, or `trial_from_plan=true`. These parameters remove the existing pending update, even if their values match the pending changes.
+- A later subscription update conflicts with discount or cancellation changes in the pending update. A conflict can occur when you provide `discounts`, the legacy `coupon` or `promotion_code` parameter, `cancel_at_period_end`, or `cancel_at`.
+  - For discount conflicts, Stripe compares discount IDs and their order, not coupon or promotion code IDs. Resubmitting a coupon or promotion code counts as a new discount, even if you use the same code. Removing a discount that the pending update adds or changes also counts as a conflict. Reusing the same discount IDs in the same order doesn’t cause a conflict.
 
